{
  "formId": "2021-03-001",
  "formTitle": "Travel Pass Application Form",
  "documentType": "application_request",
  "availability": "active",
  "checkoutEligible": null,
  "checkoutEligibleNote": "Not yet decided -- same open business-classification question as the other mapped forms. This mapping covers field-level automation only; checkout eligibility is a separate business decision.",
  "reproductionRightsVerified": true,
  "reproductionRightsNote": "Confirmed directly on the form itself: 'This document may be reproduced and is NOT FOR SALE'. Also independently confirmed by the existing R2 inventory (bi-forms-library/inventory/forms-library-inventory.json): reproduction=\"may_be_reproduced\".",
  "pageWidthPt": 612,
  "pageHeightPt": 936,
  "sourcePdf": "original.pdf",
  "derivedFrom": "Measured programmatically from a 300 DPI raster of the real original PDF (downloaded from the private fis-bi-forms-library R2 bucket, originals/2021-03-001.pdf), by detecting actual horizontal/vertical grid-line pixel darkness (meanDark~168, consistent with the other mapped forms) cross-checked against pdftotext -bbox label positions, and by direct pixel-ruled visual inspection for every structurally ambiguous region (the 4 Section I visa-type checkboxes, the Gender/Marital-Status checkboxes, and critically the apparent 'two-column' rows -- an early reading of the column-divider scan for the Applicant's Status/Date of Latest Admission row showed a single unbroken 39-cell grid, which a direct pixel-ruled crop then revealed was actually TWO separate boxes sharing a coincidentally identical column pitch, not one continuous box; the same two-box split (at the FULLGRID column 21 boundary) was then applied consistently to the Date of Intended Departure/Destination, Flight Number/Passport No., Date of Intended Return/Estimated Length, and both ACR/ICR Place-of-Issuance/Date-of-Issuance rows).",
  "measurementNotes": {
    "entirelyCustomerSupplied": "Unlike every other form mapped so far (CCS-A-CDR-2016, 2014-13-002, 2014-13-006, CCS-A-NTSP-2016, 2014-08-015 -- all of which have at least one BI-staff-only section: a certification purpose statement, a staff verification block, or both), this form's own text has NO staff-only data-entry section at all. It is a sworn, self-declared application ('The undersigned aliens hereby makes this sworn application...') ending directly in the applicant's own Date/Signature -- confirmed by reading the complete form text top to bottom, not assumed. Every field in this mapping is therefore customer-supplied, and customerPreviewCropBox covers the full page (there is no staff-only region to crop out).",
    "twoColumnRowDiscovery": "See derivedFrom above -- caught by directly inspecting a pixel-ruled crop of the Applicant's Status/Date of Latest Admission row before finalizing any coordinate for it, exactly as this directive requires, rather than trusting the column-divider scan's output at face value.",
    "dobContinuousGridWithGaps": "This form's Date of Birth comb-box (unlike CCS-A-CDR-2016/CCS-A-NTSP-2016/2014-08-015, which draw DD/MMM/YYYY as three visually separate boxes with real blank gaps) draws all 11 cells (2 for DD, 1 blank, 3 for MMM, 1 blank, 4 for YYYY) inside a single unbroken outer border -- confirmed by both the column scan (12 continuous dividers, no gap) and a direct visual crop. The blank-separator cells are structurally skipped (not assigned to any field) by splitting the 12-divider array into three sub-arrays rather than treating it as one field.",
    "maritalStatusAndGenderCheckboxes": "The 4 Section I visa-type checkboxes were measured directly (min-darkness scan tolerant of their dashed borders). The Gender M/F checkboxes were initially estimated from label proportions rather than directly measured, and the first generated test PDF showed the real bug this caused: the F mark rendered floating in the blank space between the M and F text labels, inside neither checkbox. Re-measured directly from a pixel-ruled crop of the real original (genderM box: 261.6-280.8pt x / 480.48-494.88pt y; genderF box: 290.4-304.8pt x, same y) and confirmed correct in a regenerated test PDF -- both marks now land inside their real printed boxes. The 6 Marital Status checkboxes use the same label-proportion-derived estimate (not yet independently re-verified against a pixel-ruled crop the way Gender was, since the regenerated test PDF showed the Married mark landing correctly inside its box on the first try) and remain as estimated coordinates.",
    "reasonForLeavingXStartCorrection": "A first automated pass set reasonForLeaving's xStartPt to 98.64pt, taken from the leftmost dark pixel found scanning its underline row -- which turned out to be picking up the 'Leaving:' label's own descender, not the start of the blank underline. The first generated test PDF showed the sample answer text rendering directly against the colon with no gap ('Leaving:To return home...'). Corrected to 112pt (a few points past the label's own measured xMax of 105.45pt, per pdftotext -bbox) and confirmed correct -- a visible gap -- in the regenerated test PDF."
  },
